  "prompt": "An extreme close-up photograph capturing a rugged, weather-beaten American frontiersman with calloused, grimy hands, powerfully snapping a rusty, forged metal horse spur in two with intense exertion and a determined, gritty grimace. His distressed red leather jacket and shirt are sweat-drenched and worn. Sweat and dirt are visible on his skin. The setting is the besieged, burning, and battle-torn fortifications of San Antonio at night. The iconic Alamo mission structure is silhouetted against a chaotic sky with massive fires, thick smoke plumes, distant explosions, cannons, and tiny figures of distant soldiers engaging in combat. The cinematic quality is epic and intense. Strong volumetric lighting, dramatic high-contrast chiaroscuro lighting from multiple fire sources and a distant moon creates dynamic textures on the aged metal, rough leather, and grimy hands. Deep shadows and harsh light. Heavily textured film grain, realistic textures of torn leather, fractured metal, and grit. Photorealistic, dynamic composition, last stand atmosphere, raw power, extreme detail, masterwork. Shot on an ARRI Alexa. --ar 9:16",
